    "body": "I don't think this is the right venue for this question, but nevertheless, LLMs can ingest HTML and should have trouble reading DSD; it's just HTML. They might run into issues if you're using e.g. devtools MCP to read the browsers rendered DOM, as that won't include DSD - they'll be reified into ShadowRoots, and the LLM will need to understand that and look into individual shadowRoots. All this is to say it's going to depend a lot on your particular setup or the tooling behind the scenes for a website like ChatGPT. Perhaps it's something to raise with those vendors.\n\nThere's nothing actionable for us here, so I am going to close this issue as not planned.",
